# rclone exclude list for gdrive-sync (INI format) — TEMPLATE.
# Copy to ./gdrive-exclude.conf (gitignored) and edit with your Drive's paths.
# LOCAL ONLY: ./gdrive-exclude.conf holds Drive file paths (business-sensitive,
# PII) and is deliberately NOT committed — keep this template generic.
#
# [<drive name>]   section: the patterns below apply ONLY to that shared drive,
#                  matched by name. Name the section exactly as the drive
#                  appears in Drive; the wrapper resolves the name to the drive
#                  id at runtime (from `rclone backend drives`).
# [*]              special section: patterns apply to EVERY drive (use for
#                  content types you never want from any drive, e.g. *.tmp).
# Patterns are passed VERBATIM to rclone --exclude-from (rclone-native):
#   no "/"  -> matches the basename at ANY depth (file.pdf, *glob*, *.tmp,
#              or a lone "*" = every file in the section);
#   "/"     -> matches the full path relative to the drive root
#              (sub/dir/file.pdf).
# Per-drive entries are for permanently non-downloadable files: Drive-admin
# download-forbidden (403 cannotDownloadFile / 'forbidden to download') or
# dangling shortcuts (target gone). Append an entry when a sync fails fast on a
# new non-downloadable file; delete it only when the file becomes downloadable.
# Transient errors (network/5xx) are NOT listed here — those fail-fast.
# The sync report includes a "Files excluded" section listing the Drive files
# that matched these patterns (parsed from rclone's DEBUG log).

[*]
*.tmp
*.pyc
*.py
*.csv
*.s
*.c
*.h
*.inc
*.cfg

[<drive name>]
some-file.pdf
some-glob*.*
sub/dir/file.pdf